@startuml
hide footbox
title Conditional static transaction scenario - runtime identity UNKNOWN
actor "Scenario entry" as Entry
participant "Other" as B1
participant "Review" as B2
legend left
All P identifiers are SYMBOLIC_SCENARIO; actual runtime identity UNKNOWN.
L = TRANSACTION_LOGICAL_SCOPE; P = TRANSACTION_PHYSICAL
S = TRANSACTION_SUSPENDED; SP = TRANSACTION_SAVEPOINT
Green: shared physical context / logical scope
Blue: independent physical scope; outer P retained while SUSPENDED
Yellow: nested SAVEPOINT on the SAME P
Gray: NO_TRANSACTION; red: UNKNOWN / unsupported path
Groups show method nesting. BEGIN/END notes define physical lifetimes.
Suspended lifetime overlap is explicit in SUSPEND/RESUME notes.
Interception: APPLIED / BYPASSED / UNKNOWN; context: ACTIVE / INACTIVE / UNKNOWN.
INHERITED physical context does not require interception of this method.
AspectJ ASSUMED_APPLIED is a conditional premise, never runtime weaving proof.
endlegend
Entry -> B2: Review#outer() / CONDITIONAL_CALL
group #CCE5FF F1 REQUIRED L1 P1
note right of B2: interception=APPLIED; context=ACTIVE; INDEPENDENT P1
note right of B2: advice=SCENARIO_PROXY_CALL; manager=tx
note over B2: 2 PHYSICAL_BEGIN P1 
note over B2: 3 LOGICAL_BEGIN L1 
note right of B2 #FFCCCC: UNKNOWN call System.gc; remaining order NOT ASSERTED
B2 -> B1: Other#inner() / CONDITIONAL_CALL
group #D6F5D6 F2 REQUIRED L2 P1
note right of B1: interception=APPLIED; context=ACTIVE; INHERITED P1
note right of B1: advice=SCENARIO_PROXY_CALL; manager=tx
note over B1: 6 LOGICAL_BEGIN L2 
note over B1: 7 LOGICAL_END L2 
end
B1 --> B2: scope exit / outcome UNKNOWN
note over B2: 9 LOGICAL_END L1 
note over B2: 10 PHYSICAL_END_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN P1 
end
B2 --> Entry: attempt/path end UNKNOWN
@enduml
